<title>USA: Allied Signal patents challenged by DSM.</title>
<headline>Allied Signal patents challenged by DSM.</headline>
<dateline>WILMINGTON, Del. 1997-03-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>DSM High Performance Fibers B.V. of Sittard, The Netherlands, has challenged the validity of two patents owned by AlliedSignal Inc, according to court papers.</p>
<p>In papers filed Monday in the U.S. District Court in Delaware, DSM alleged that the patents related to low-shrink, high-tenacity polyolefin fiber and the process for producing it were &quot;invalid&quot;.</p>
<p>DSM is a unit of DSM NV.</p>
<p>The basis for the invalidity allegation was not described in court papers.</p>
<p>DSM seeks a court ruling supporting its claim of invalidity, the court papers said.</p>
